# Volute — Controls

This file fixes the input contract: the actions the game reads, what each one is
bound to, how the injector's aim is steered, and which actions each screen
answers. Keyboard and mouse are the whole input surface.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
## Where input reaches the game

This game stands on no engine, so the input layer is yours to write. It binds
keys by `KeyboardEvent.code`, so a binding is a physical key whatever the
keyboard layout, and it reports each action two ways: as a held value, true
while any of its keys is down, and as a press edge, true once for the frame in
which the held value became true. A key event whose `repeat` flag is set arms no
edge. The layer reports the pointer position in the field's logical units and
tells the primary and secondary mouse buttons apart.

## Actions and bindings

| Action | Keys | Mouse | Read as | Does |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| turn left | `ArrowLeft` | — | held | turns the aim counter-clockwise |
| turn right | `ArrowRight` | — | held | turns the aim clockwise |
| fire | `Space` | primary button | edge | fires the loaded core along the aim |
| swap | `KeyX` | secondary button | edge | exchanges the loaded and queued cores |
| confirm | `Enter`, `Space` | — | edge | starts a run, and dismisses an ending |
| pause | `Escape` | — | edge | pauses, and resumes |
| mute | `KeyM` | — | edge | toggles the audio between muted and unmuted |

`Space` carries both fire and confirm, and the two never answer on the same
screen. Mute answers on every screen. The backtick, `Backquote`, toggles the
debug overlay on every screen and sits outside the table.

The field answers a secondary press as a control, leaving the browser's context
menu closed.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
## Where input reaches the game

The {{engine.name}} engine owns the keyboard and the pointer, and the
documentation it ships in `engine/` defines how an action is registered and
read. The build registers every action `ACTIONS` names, under the keys
`BINDINGS` binds it to, and reads the pointer's position for the aim and its
press edge for the shot.

## Actions

| Action | Read as | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `left` | held | turns the aim counter-clockwise |
| `right` | held | turns the aim clockwise |
| `a` | edge | fires the loaded core along the aim |
| `b` | edge | exchanges the loaded and queued cores |
| `confirm` | edge | starts a run, and dismisses an ending |
| `pause` | edge | pauses, and resumes |
| `mute` | edge | toggles the audio between muted and unmuted |

A pointer press raises `a`, so a shot leaves the injector where the pointer put
the aim. `Space` is bound to both `a` and `confirm`, and the two never answer on
the same screen. `mute` answers on every screen. `up`, `down`, and `back` come
with the layout and drive nothing. The backtick toggles the engine's debug
overlay on every screen.
{{else}}
## Where input reaches the game

The {{engine.name}} engine owns the keyboard and the pointer, and the
documentation it ships in `engine/` defines how an action is registered and read
through a player controller. The build registers every action `ACTIONS` names,
under the binding `BINDINGS` gives it, and reads the pointer's position for the
aim and its press edge for the shot.

## Actions

| Action | Read as | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `aim-left` | held | turns the aim counter-clockwise |
| `aim-right` | held | turns the aim clockwise |
| `fire` | edge | fires the loaded core along the aim |
| `swap` | edge | exchanges the loaded and queued cores |
| `confirm` | edge | starts a run, and dismisses an ending |
| `pause` | edge | pauses, and resumes |
| `mute` | edge | toggles the audio between muted and unmuted |

A pointer press raises `fire`, so a shot leaves the injector where the pointer
put the aim. `Space` is bound to both `fire` and `confirm`, and the two never
answer on the same screen. `mute` answers on every screen. The backtick toggles
the engine's debug overlay on every screen.
{{/if}}

## Aiming

An update resolves the pointer first and the turn actions second. A pointer
position delivered that update sets the aim to the angle from the injector's
center to that position, and a pointer position exactly at the injector's center
leaves the aim unchanged. A held turn action then turns the aim by 180 degrees
for every second of simulation time the update advances, counter-clockwise on
screen for turn left and clockwise for turn right, and the two held together
turn the aim by nothing.

## Firing and swapping

Fire and swap each raise one request on the press edge, so a held control raises
no further request until it is released and pressed again.
Both are live on `playing` alone, and the frame that raises a request is the
frame that consumes it.

## What each screen reads

| Screen | Live |
| --- | --- |
| `title` | confirm starts a run |
| `playing` | the pointer, the two turn actions, fire, swap, and pause, which pauses |
| `paused` | pause, which resumes |
| `cleared`, `setback` | nothing; the interlude runs on its own timer |
| `gameover`, `victory` | confirm dismisses the ending |

An action a row omits does nothing on that screen. Mute is live on every screen.
